think Loaded the voice first (KYRI, RADIANT_STYLE), then REMEMBER, REDS, the itineraries by reference, and the top rows of session-logs/README.md to catch the baton. The watershed log (143054) is the newest edge; its recommend named three crux-first siblings -- a disk-element builder, a size histogram, and an AUTO-MARKER seeder that runs watershed end-to-end off a bare mask.
think Standfast check: every living REDS row (80, 83, 84, 85, 86, 87) is closed or released; only #75 rests as custody-gated errata. No agent-closable red blocks new work, so the line is clear to grow the live family.
think Crux-first among the three siblings: the auto-marker seeder is the highest-Lindy (it turns the whole distance/medial/label/watershed family into an end-to-end tool -- the thing every count/separate-touching-cells task descends from) AND a real crux (the classic hard part of watershed is choosing the markers). It is the capstone the arc was explicitly built toward: distance's doc names a watershed, medial_axis's doc names the watershed as what its ridge seeds, watershed's doc names the medial ridge as exactly where a marker belongs.
think Read the four building blocks for exact APIs (measurement beats memory): distance.distance_chamfer -> DistanceMap{width,height,max_distance,dist,at}; medial_axis.medial_mask/is_ridge (local-maxima ridge, plateaus kept); label.label_components -> LabelMap{count,labels,at} + label_color; watershed.watershed(field, markers) + colorize + is_watershed. The pipeline is pure compose: markers = label_components(medial_mask(distance_chamfer(mask))), then watershed(field, markers).
think Hand-traced the crux shape before coding. A 1-tall neck fails (its pixels form a flat depth-3 ridge plateau -> a spurious third marker). Two 3x3 blocks touching only at a CORNER works clean: (2,2) and (5,5) each read depth 6, the shallow corner touch (3,3)/(4,4) reads depth 3 (not a local max, so never a ridge), so the ridge is two disconnected single pixels -> exactly TWO markers -> the flood splits the one 8-connected component into two basins with a watershed line at the touch.
think Verified the UNIFORM-BAR contrast by hand: the 9-wide 3-tall bar (the watershed witness's own shape) has one connected depth-ridge along its middle (interior depth 6, ends depth 3), so auto-markers finds ONE marker and segment keeps it whole -- to split a bar you must hand-seat markers, which is what watershed is for. Auto-markers respects true object structure rather than inventing a cut. That contrast is the honest heart of the rung.
obs Built image/segment.rye with three verbs -- markers_of_field (the crux: ridge -> connected components -> dense basins), auto_markers (convenience over a mask), segment (end-to-end, distance built once) -- plus a tools/segment_witness.rish. Compose not braid: the module owns only the marker-selection choice and the wiring; distance/medial_axis/label/watershed own the rest, no new gather/loop/blend/codec/color.
obs GREEN on the FIRST metal run, no reds. Cruxes proven: AUTO-SPLIT (one 8-connected component -> two basins from a bare mask, corner never seeded), PARITY (segment == distance -> markers_of_field -> watershed byte-for-byte, the wiring proven not a black box), SINGLE-BLOB (lone block whole, no line), UNIFORM-BAR (bar stays one basin under auto-markers), colorize QOI round-trip, two refusals by name (EmptySource, NoMarkers), determinism.
obs The honest over-segmentation boundary is named in code, README, card, and log rather than hidden (as medial_axis names its non-unit-width): a single object with several distinct distance peaks can over-segment, one basin per peak; the h-maxima remedy that merges shallow peaks is the named horizon, a later sibling, not built here. That horizon is now the crux-first next sibling in REMEMBER.
obs TAME bans clean, width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII, living-docs exit 0, living-card ASCII witness GREEN. image/README.md names segment.rye after watershed (docs-sync in the same commit). REMEMBER repointed single-stranded -- segment lifted to the live edge and git nib, watershed folded to a one-line prior-nib comment (no cairn -- a one-line repoint, no living-card body swept).
obs Council rota lap deep-read follow-our-compass (item 2, cycling 27 -> 1 -> 2 by lap index): witness before narrative, one lap one witness bolt, brief and green witnesses win. Applied directly -- this lap took the single highest-Lindy crux, proved it GREEN on metal before any prose claimed it landed, and repointed the plan to match.
